-All elements of a vector parameter must be specified in the `data.frame`, even if some values do not change across scenarios (e.g., `hiv.test.rate_2` is constant here but must still be included).
+A column sets only its own position: the positions of a vector parameter without a column keep their current value, both before the simulation and when an updater applies the row during it. Here, `hiv.test.rate_2` could be left out if the base parameter object already holds 0.001 in that position. A column without a position suffix (`hiv.test.rate`) replaces the whole vector with its single value. Positions past the end of the current vector extend it when they leave no gap (`hiv.test.rate_4` alone extends a vector of length 3, while `hiv.test.rate_5` alone is an error), and a scenario cannot shorten a vector. Before EpiModel 2.7.0, the columns of a scenario replaced the whole vector, so every position had to be given.
 
